    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0745" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg633"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador O’Brien to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-08-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>See memorandum with my 1160, May 10 last. Japanese Government unable to reconcile
                    additional protocol with their recommendation. Do you understand that under it
                    and independently of constitutional difficulties Japan has the right to limit
                    recourse against her in international court to action for damages? Right of
                    reservation seems not to be general.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
